1. MATERIAL IN THIS REPOSITORY'S SOURCE
=========================================

BLAKE3 reference implementation (Motoko port)
  kernels/moxzi-hash/src/internal/Blake3Ref.mo is a direct port to Motoko of the official
  BLAKE3 reference implementation,
  https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3/blob/master/reference_impl/reference_impl.rs
  Copyright the BLAKE3 authors (Jack O'Connor, Jean-Philippe Aumasson, Samuel Neves,
  Zooko Wilcox-O'Hearn). Used under CC0-1.0 (public domain dedication); also available
  under Apache-2.0.

Ed25519 (RFC 8032) in Motoko, from mo:ic-agent
  kernels/moxzi-ed25519/src/internal/Ed25519Ref.mo is a verbatim copy of src/Ed25519.mo of
  mo:ic-agent 0.2.0 (https://github.com/icdevsorg/ic-agent-mo), Copyright ICDevs.org,
  published under Apache-2.0 and offered here by the same copyright holder under this
  repository's licenses.

Test vectors (used only by the check crates; never part of a kernel)
  kernels/moxzi-rsa/check/vectors/wycheproof-rsa_pss_3072_sha256_mgf1_32.json
  kernels/moxzi-secp256k1/check/vectors/wycheproof-ecdsa-secp256k1-sha256-bitcoin.json
    Project Wycheproof, https://github.com/C2SP/wycheproof. Copyright Google LLC and the
    Wycheproof authors. Apache-2.0. The secp256k1 file is reduced to the fields the checks
    read (key, tcId, msg, sig, result).
  kernels/moxzi-secp256k1/check/vectors/bip340-test-vectors.csv
    BIP 340 test vectors, https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0340/test-vectors.csv
    (BIP 340: BSD-2-Clause).
  kernels/moxzi-kernel/check/vectors/kernel-family-bitcoin.json
    A selection from (the file's "_sources" field names each part):
    - Bitcoin Core test data (src/test/data/key_io_valid.json, key_io_invalid.json,
      sighash.json), https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin, Copyright The Bitcoin Core
      developers, MIT.
    - BIP 32 (BSD-2-Clause), BIP 143 (public domain) and BIP 341 (BSD-3-Clause) test vectors,
      https://github.com/bitcoin/bips.

Specifications implemented (no code copied): FIPS 204 (ML-DSA), FIPS 202 (SHA-3/SHAKE),
FIPS 180-4, RFC 2104, RFC 6979, RFC 8017, RFC 8032, RFC 9380, SEC 1, BIP 32, BIP 173,
BIP 340, BIP 341, BIP 350.

The Motoko packages depend on further mops packages (mo:base, mo:core, mo:sha2, mo:bitcoin,
mo:bls12-381); those are fetched from the mops registry under their own licenses and are not
part of this repository.


2. CODE COMPILED INTO THE KERNELS
==================================

Each kernel/*.kernel.toml file embeds a compiled WebAssembly module. Besides this
repository's own code, that module contains compiled code from the Rust crates below (the
normal dependencies of the kernel crates for the kernel target, resolved from each crate's
committed Cargo.lock; link-time optimisation keeps only the code a kernel reaches), and from
the Rust standard library's `core` and `alloc` and `compiler_builtins` (built with
-Zbuild-std; MIT OR Apache-2.0, compiler_builtins including LLVM compiler-rt code under
Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception). This repository does not include the dependencies' source;
cargo fetches it from crates.io when a kernel is built.

Every license below is permissive and compatible with distributing this repository's source
under MIT OR Apache-2.0 and the compiled kernels with this notice. Where a crate offers a
choice, the kernels use it under the MIT or Apache-2.0 option.

